{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/440323-sacred-hunt-gift-overlap","id":440323,"title":"Sacred Hunt / Gift overlap","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-13T12:47:24-07:00","id":440323,"title":"Sacred Hunt / Gift overlap","content":"A conversation in the errata thread started this train of thought, but it could use its own thread.<br /> By and large, the powers granted by the various Tribes to those who are on the sacred hunt are unique. There doesn't seem to be any other gift or whatever that would let someone picked out spirit-ridden or urged than the Storm Lord Siskur-Dah.<br /> <br /> The big one that does have overlap is the Iron Masters extra skill. Glorious Lunacy and the Wisdom Facet of the Rage Gift both let you cause a specific kind of Lunacy to everyone, and Gaze of the Moon lets you cause a specific and typical type to one person. Sure, these cause essence, but Awestruck on everyone is arguably more useful than any of the three Conditions that Lunacy normally causes.<br /> <br /> Does anyone think this is worth taking a second look at to give Iron Masters a more unique human-hunting power?<br /> Or for that matter, does anyone see any other significant such overlaps?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}